== ui_card "Quick Start Guide"
  p Welcome to Slim-Pickins! This guide will get you up and running with the framework in less than 5 minutes.

  h3 1. Installation
  p Add the gem to your <code>Gemfile</code>:
  
  pre style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px;"
    code gem "slim-pickins"
    
  p And run:
  pre style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px;"
    code bundle install
    
  h3 2. Asset Setup
  p Slim-Pickins relies on <strong>Stimulus</strong> for interactivity and <strong>SortableJS</strong> for drag-and-drop lists.
  p Ensure your application loads these libraries. For a standard import-map setup:
  
  pre style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px;"
    code
      | // application.js
        import "@hotwired/stimulus"
        import "sortablejs"
        // The gem automatically registers its controllers if using the engine
        
  h3 3. Configuration
  p In your main application file (e.g., <code>app.rb</code> for Sinatra), register the extension:
  
  pre style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px;"
    code
      | class App < Sinatra::Base
          register SlimPickins
          # ...
        end

  h3 4. Your First Component
  p Now you can use the helpers in your Slim templates!
  
  .sp-card style="border-left: 4px solid var(--sp-primary);"
    .sp-card__body
      h4 Example: User Profile Card
      p Copy and paste this into any view:
      
      pre style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 1rem;"
        code
          | == ui_card "User Profile" do
              .sp-cluster
                span Name: Jane Doe
                == ui_button "Edit", :neutral
  
  h3 Next Steps
  p Ready to build? Explore the core components:
  
  .sp-cluster
    a.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary href="/docs/button" Buttons
    a.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary href="/docs/card" Cards
    a.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary href="/docs/form" Forms
